* Sum component reference -- the "## Example" netlist verbatim.
* No title line -- see doc-verify/const/example.cir's own comment for why.
*
* ERR is the classic error junction: signs=1,-1 makes it A - B = 3 - 1 = 2.
* VSUM shows the vector rule: all-vector inputs of one common length (here 2) reduce
* elementwise, so VSUM = OA + OB = [1+10, 2+20] = [11, 22] (see
* test_sum.py::test_example_scalar_error_junction_and_vector_sum).
A kind=const value=3
B kind=const value=1
ERR kind=sum inputs=A,B signs=1,-1
OA kind=const value=[1,2]
OB kind=const value=[10,20]
VSUM kind=sum inputs=OA,OB signs=1,1
